#!/bin/sh
# WolOS live (ISO, ADR 0009): the root is read-only cd9660. Writable state lives in memory (tmpfs,
# unionfs over /etc and /usr/local/etc; /var and /tmp are rc's memory disks). Never touches a disk.
# Any other root (installed system, rw USB stick) is left alone.
set -u
R=${WOLOS_LIVE_ROOT:-}
[ "$(mount -p | awk '$2=="/"{print $3; exit}')" = cd9660 ] || exit 0
logger -t wolos_live "live boot: memory overlays" 2>/dev/null || :
for d in /etc /usr/local/etc; do
  u=$R/var/run/wolos-live$d; mkdir -p "$u"
  mount -t tmpfs tmpfs "$u" && mount -t unionfs "$u" "$R$d"
done
mount -t tmpfs tmpfs "$R/home"
mkdir -p "$R/home/live"
chown -R 1000:1000 "$R/home/live"
